# fig_breakeven

**Claim carried:** C3: learning a calibrator from the same labels pays only above a break-even n, which the formula predicts.

**Shows:** width of the cross-fitted calibrated interval divided by PPI++ width (paired) against the number of labels n, per dataset and calibrator, with 95% CI band; dotted line and shaded band = predicted n* with its interval; text = predicted n* lies outside the plotted grid. The last panel (C1) is predicted against measured excess width over the floor.

**How to read:** crossing of the curve through 1 should sit at the dotted line if the formula holds; a curve that never crosses in the grid means n* was not reached there. Last panel: both axes as a fraction of the floor width (filled = synthetic cell, hollow centre = real dataset), identity dashed; points on it, within their CI, mean the closed-form gap holds; estimators without a closed form are not drawn. Panels shown: gene expr., census income, alphafold, galaxies, syn quad c0.05, syn quad c0.2, syn binary; the others are in fig_breakeven_all_a (the nine real datasets) and fig_breakeven_all_b (monotone-transformed predictors and synthetic designs).

